  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation  $3\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=20-\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x$ for ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x & =20-\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x & =20 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}\u2061x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\text{arctan}(\\frac{1}{5})=(11.309\\,9\u2026)^{\u2218}\u2248{11.310}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${11.310}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={11.310}^{\u2218}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{\u2218}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}={180}^{\u2218}+{11.310}^{\u2218}={191.310}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is\n\n$$\n11.310\\cdot 191.310\u22482\\,164\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.",
